A||||5||pontiacs4me||Jumping off the turbo bandwagon!||||1||
Z||000000||pontiacs4me||09-10-2001||01:42 AM||||Awhile back I asked a bunch of questions about building up a 3.4 with a t3/t4 hybrid and all that.  Then after visiting a local salvage yard that has hundreds of GM cars, without 1 3.4, but about 15 3.8 liters, I decided on building one of them with a t3/t4.  Then I started adding up prices.  With the intercooler, the turbo, computer upgrades, engine parts, etc, etc, I figured / $4500 minumum.  <BR>well I have this good friend that put an L67 3800 supercharged in his 91 lumina.  that car is incredible, and he did the swap for just under $5000.  He told me if he could do it again, he could do it for less than 3, so theres where im going.  Ive put my dreams of Stage II on standby.  I hope to have the engine and tranny by November, and have the swap complete by mid January.  Im going to be setting up a website (im not releasing the site name until its paid for, because it is really cool) explaining everything necessary for the swap, building custom headers, and fabricating axles.  <BR>Just thought Id let everyone know, I jumped off the turbo bandwagon, and jumped on the supercharger one.<P>One more thing, check out <A HREF="http://www.luminasupercharged.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.luminasupercharged.com</A>  this is my friend that will be helping me with the swap.<p>[This message has been edited by pontiacs4me (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||09-10-2001||02:02 AM||||I was gonna ask if that was your friends site.. that car is awesome!  sleepers rule!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||pontiacs4me||09-10-2001||02:09 AM||||yeah that is my friend Tom, I painted that car last year.  I love that car, it is so fun.  Especially when we pull up next to some old man in a new vette, flex on him a bit, he looks over, laughs at us, then when the light turns green the guy in the vette thinks hes going to speed away making fools of us.  All of a sudden we pull on him and make him feel like the jackass.  A 4 door lumina killing a $35,000 car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||09-10-2001||01:57 PM||||That's great! That's one awesome car!<BR>I've always kinda liked that generation of Lumina, anyway. The 3800 makes it a killer.<BR>Good luck with yours.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000004||sqoach||09-10-2001||02:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pontiacs4me:<BR><B>A 4 door lumina killing a $35,000 car.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Correction: $50,000 car.<BR>Haven't you seen the price tags on these brand new vettes?<P>Anyway, a 3800 is something I kinda want(ed) to do down the road. But I've heard the 3.4 being much easier to swap. Since I know jack about engine swapping, I'm leaning toward the 3.4 because it's easier/cheaper. But I may change my mind. Who knows. I have a question though. What's the differences in the 3800 and the 3800SC? I'm sure the SC has more hp/torque. But do you have any numbers? Is one easier than the other?<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">        <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC (FOR SALE)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||pontiacs4me||09-11-2001||01:40 AM||||the series II 3800 natural aspirated makes 205 hp and the supercharged version makes 240 horsepower.   The NA makes 240 ft lbs and the SC makes 280 ft lbs.  With easy bolt on mods the supercharged version can make 275 horse for a couple hundred bucks.  It takes major mods on the NA version to pull that.  Toms lumina is probably pulling 375 horse now, but thats with a 75 shot of N2O.  His car is in the high 12's now, and gets 24+ mpg on the highway.  With the same setup on my fiero weighing 770 lbs less,  that will put me at around 12.1 in the 1/4.  and 24+ mpg.||||reg||1
